      "embeddings": "not on the NPU yet: OpenVINO Model Server 2026 serves embeddings on the NPU as a preview (OpenVINO/Qwen3-Embedding-0.6B-int8-ov, --task embeddings --pooling LAST), untried here; until the NPU check has tried it on hardware they go to the graphics card or the processor",
      "vision": "none on the NPU yet: OpenVINO's Qwen3-VL-4B INT4 build is asymmetric, which the NPU doesn't take; vision goes to the graphics card or the processor",
      "licence": "OpenVINO Model Server: Apache-2.0",
      "notes": "A zip, unpacked into the tools home: no installer, no administrator. Its programs need the Microsoft Visual C++ runtime, which its zip doesn't carry (only its Python's vcruntime140): setup copies the five DLLs they import from Microsoft's own CRT package (runtime, pinned) beside ovms.exe, where Windows loads them first, so no administrator installs the Redistributable (run on a Lunar Lake, 2026-10-12). It needs Intel's NPU driver 32.0.100.4023 or later. It serves the OpenAI routes at /v1 (and the older /v3), source-checked at v2026.4.1. The NPU compiles a model on first load (minutes), cached in --cache_dir. Its zip wraps everything in an ovms folder, which setup unpacks into ovms-2026.4.1; its Python (for chat templates) needs PYTHONHOME and PATH, which the entry's env gives (its setupvars script does the same). Its model is a channel-wise INT4 export (symmetric, one scale per output channel), the kind the NPU runs properly: the group-wise AWQ export it had first, OpenVINO's Qwen3-4B-int4-ov, loads and answers fast on a Lunar Lake NPU, but nonsense (\"?option?option…\"), while answering properly on the same PC's processor and graphics card (2026-10-12). OpenVINO publishes channel-wise exports of other models (Qwen3-8B-int4-cw-ov, 4.7 GB, also answered properly there, at 14.8 tokens a second) but none of a Qwen3 4B, so Castellan made one of Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507 (optimum-cli export openvino --weight-format int4 --sym --ratio 1.0 --group-size -1; its model card has the versions) and publishes it as Castellan-AI/Qwen3-4B-Instruct-2507-int4-cw-ov, its files pinned for every generation (OpenVINO's model is the same file on each: each PC compiles it for its own NPU). The NPU check with it on that Lunar Lake (Core Ultra 7 256V, NPU driver 32.0.100.4512, 2026-10-12), every step passed: the first load with its compile 31 s, from its cache 4 s; 26 tokens written and about 670 read a second; a short answer warm in 0.7 s; 1,395 tokens answered and 1,792 refused plainly (400) at --max_prompt_len 1536, the server still up; two requests at once both answered; 3.6 GB working set. The timeouts leave room for Meteor Lake's slower NPU 3720, not yet measured (the check suggested base 10 s, 100 ms a token, cold load 60 s on Lunar Lake)."
    },
